\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1208305 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Chapter 2: Overview of Literature}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2249970 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1208305 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 2.1 Overview of Literature
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid13451543 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13451543 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
There has been substantial research dedicated to applying artificial intelligence (AI) for detecting lung cancer in patients due to the vast amount of deaths from delayed diagnosis or diagnosis in later stages of lung cancer. CT imaging has been shown to 
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
be a reliable source of determining early-stage lung cancer; however, the amount of time spent on generating medical-related information from CT scans is substantial and subject to human error during interpretation. The development of deep learning method
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 s,\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  in particular, convolutional neural networks (CNNs), has created an option to use automated methods for extracting features from the CT image and classifying them accurately.

\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
The goal of this chapter is two-fold: first, it will describe the current knowledge of AI being used to detect lung cancer; second, it will provide an extensive discussion of why AI is challenging to use in the imaging arena. Finally, it will identify gap
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 s in the existing literature that can be addressed through this project.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1208305 .
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid1208305 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1208305 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
2.2 The Use of Deep Learning Techniques in the Analysis of Medical Images
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13451543\charrsid13451543 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Medical image analysis is being revolutionized by the use of deep-learning techniques (e.g., Convolutional Neural Networks). Rather than requiring that humans manually extract the features from images, CNNs perform the process of feature extraction automa
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 tically. Pre-trained CNN architectures (e.g., VGGNet, ResNet & EfficientNet) have demonstrated success on a variety of medical imaging applications, including lung nodule detection/classification/segmentation.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13451543 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1208305 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
The results of numerous studies indicate that CNN-based models are capable of providing highly accurate results and assist radiologists by improving their diagnostic efficacy. However, many studies are limited by using clean and/or curated datasets. As a 
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 result, the generalizability of CNN-based models is limited in practical clinical environments.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid1208305 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10038949 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2249970 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10038949 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 2.3 AI lung cancer detection
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid12781731\charrsid12781731 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
AI can be used to detect lung cancer through the following steps: imaging precursors, segmentation, feature extraction and classification. The` image classification and processing` stages usually have a classification accuracy of 90% classifying at least 
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 on public data sets like LIDC-IDRI. The models can also assist in providing early diagnosis of lung cancer.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid12781731 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13451543\charrsid13451543 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
The classification accuracy mentioned above is largely based on the fact that the CT images contain new properties. However, in a clinical setting, the quality of a CT image may be different depending on whether the CT image was recorded in a manner that 
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 created degradation, partial slices, or noise.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13451543 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13451543\charrsid13451543 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 2.4 Existing AI-based lung cancer detection systems with lower lung cancer image quality 2.4.1 Image Quality Considerations}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 
\ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid13451543 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10038949 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Most non-experimental CT images have some form of "blurriness", "noise", "low contrast", or "low resolution". These problems reduce the visibility of nodules and decrease the performance of models detecting lung cancer in clinical practice. The overall im
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 pact of these deficits on the robustness of existing lung cancer detection models under real-life imaging conditions is unknown and thus has not yet been established through research.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\insrsid10038949 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2249970 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10038949 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 2.4.2 Incomplete or limited data}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2249970 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10038949 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Individual data records in the medical domain may be incomplete (or missing completely), due to HIPAA regulations, missing slices from imaging studies, or the number of records with a lung cancer diagnosis being very low. In addition to being incomplete, 
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
lung cancer records typically contain very few data records. This means that it is unlikely to be able to build models using only the provided data. Consequently, lung cancer data are often poorly represented in the sample data.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
To combat the limitations described above, using techniques such as data augmentation; transfer learning, and weighted loss functions; typically, researchers have improved the generalizability of existing AI-based lung cancer detection models when trained
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  using limited, unstructured data.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10038949 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2249970 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10038949 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 2.5 Image Pre-Processing and Enhancement
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Previous studies have examined pre-processing methods used to reduce or eliminate image degradation using the following techniques:
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 1) Gaussian filtering and Image noise removal
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 2) Contrast enhancement by histogram equalization
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 3) Image resizing and normalization
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5378393 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5378393 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Despite the improved precision of each method mentioned, there is very little knowledge on the effects of these methodologies on images blurred or incomplete from computed tomography (CT).
\par 
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 2.6 Web-Based Artificial Intelligence for Medical Imaging
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Over the past few years, many published studies have addressed web-based applications that incorporate artificial intelligence, both in research projects and clinical prototype development. These applications enable researchers and healthcare professional
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 s to coll\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
aborate on models while also allowing for the upload of images to view predicted outcomes through a web-based medium. Unfortunately, most web-based prototypes do not take into account their viability when working with images that are of low-quality or inc
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 omplete.
\par 
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Integrating AI into web-based applications has increased accessibility to solutions based on research, therefore supporting the viability of using solutions based on research in real-world applications.}{\rtlch\fcs1 
\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid2249970 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10038949 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10038949 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 2.7 Research Gap
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Although there are many studies demonstrating high accuracy of models on pristine datasets derived from lung CT images, many do not consider some of the difficulties that exist when applying a model to real world CT images:
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Blurry, noisy, or low-resolution images
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 CT images with incomplete datasets (i.e. missing slices)
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 No interactive prototype applications
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Lack of systematic evaluations of model performance under degradation/incomplete or other clinically-relevant conditions.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The proposed research solves the above research gaps by providing:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid5378393 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid5378393 \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
A strong deep learning algorithm for identifying lung cancer from poor quality and diminished CT images.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Flask-powered web app developed to serve as an interactive demonstration of this research.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Both a novel contribution to academia and furthering AI's impact on medical imaging.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10038949 .
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\sa160\sl278\slmult1\widctlpar\wrapdefault\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0\itap0\pararsid10038949 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10038949 
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 2.8 Summary
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
Deep learning has advanced the ability to detect lung cancer via CT images, but there are still issues that must be addressed before the technology can be fully applied in a clinical setting, such as degradation of the CT images and/or the CT images being
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
 incomplete due to missing slices, as well as lack of interactive prototype applications. Therefore, this research will contribute to advanced lung cancer detection via deep learning; propose an initial solution; and, develop a robust and research-oriente
\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 d\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506  prototype for lung cancer detection.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid10038949\charrsid5451033 
